    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1177">

                <pb facs="1208" n="1194" xml:id="pg1194"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.20/8–744</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Berle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chief of
                        Staff, United States Army</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Marshall</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-24">August 24,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear General</hi>: I enclose a letter from
                    Ambassador Messersmith<anchor n="26" xml:id="d1177-f1"/> regarding a possible
                    growing desire on the part of the Mexican Army ground forces to participate
                    overseas.</p>
                <p>The Ambassador gives some very pertinent background material and strongly
                    recommends that any initiative on this should come from Mexico, a recommendation
                    which seems very wise in view of all the considerations involved in this.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. A. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berle, Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1177-f1" n="26" xml:id="d1177-f1-content">
                <p>Letter dated August 7, 1944, addressed to Joseph F. McGurk, Acting Deputy
                    Director of the Office of American Republic Affairs; not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
